{{Quote|Out here, we're just one of the millions of little backwaters no one cares about.|Jaybo Hood|<ref name="Mystery of a Thousand Moons" />}}
'''Iego''' was a mysterious [[planet]] located in the [[Outer Rim Territories]] on the fringes of [[The galaxy|the known galaxy]] that was surrounded by a thousand [[moon]]s collectively known as the [[moons of Iego]], at least [[Millius Prime|one]] of which was populated by a race of beings known as [[Diathim|Angels]]. During the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] constructed a [[Laser web|laser field]] that prevented anyone from leaving the planet, before the field was destroyed by [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Anakin Skywalker]], freeing the Iegoans.<ref name="Mystery of a Thousand Moons" />

==Description==
{{Dialogue|Jaybo Hood|Follow the vines to the bottom, dig up the roots, but don't touch the vine.|Obi-Wan Kenobi|Aside from the obvious, why not?|Jaybo Hood|Because the plants don't like it, and they have big, sharp teeth.|Anakin Skywalker|Teeth? This is getting better by the minute.|Jaybo Hood|And watch out for the flying xandu.|attr=Jaybo Hood, Obi-Wan Kenobi, and Anakin Skywalker discuss the dangers of Iego|src=<ref name="Mystery of a Thousand Moons" />}}
Located on the fringes of [[The galaxy|the known galaxy]], the [[planet]] Iego was [[orbit]]ed by a thousand [[moon]]s<ref name="Iego" /> collectively known as the [[moons of Iego]],<ref name="The Phantom Menace">{{Film|I}}</ref> including [[Clepresdan]], [[Cobarb]], [[Flitrude]], [[Millius Prime]], [[Rawnde]], [[Uncovalor]], and [[Winlion]]. Each was as mysterious as the world itself. Iego was a hotbed of life and had both [[Temperature|hot]]<ref name="SWTVE" /> and temperate climates and was tropical,<ref name="Iego" /> steamy, and humid.<ref name="SWTVE" /> Its [[desert]] surface<ref name="Iego" /> was covered in [[basalt]]ic spires<ref name="Cliffhold" /> and canyons, where [[reeksa]] (enormous, ravenous carnivorous [[plant]]s with sharpened spikes for [[Tooth|teeth]] and deadly thorns along their length<ref name="Reeksa" /> that were known to eat [[human]]s alive, and whose roots were used to create the only known antidote to the [[Blue Shadow Virus]]) grew. Iego was also inhabited by [[xandu]], creatures who flew though Iego's skies on their four wings and used their giant [[ear]]s to hear prey at great distances, after which they would snatch them up and smash them against rock walls using their two [[Limb|arms]] and two legs.<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref>

==History==
{{Quote|This system is haunted, cursed, whatever. Anyway, Jedi or not, no one gets off this rock alive, not past Drol.|Jaybo Hood, to Obi-Wan Kenobi and Anakin Skywalker|<ref name="Mystery of a Thousand Moons" />}}
During the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] invaded Iego with hundreds of [[B1-series battle droid|battle droids]] and stole Millius Prime from its inhabitants, the [[Diathim]]. There, they built a [[laser web]]<ref name="MoaTMAG">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/mystery-of-a-thousand-moons-concept-art-gallery|text="Mystery of a Thousand Moons" Concept Art Gallery}}</ref> security system to prevent the inhabitants from leaving the system. The Separatists then abandoned Iego and left battle droids and [[Vulture-class starfighter|vulture droids]] behind at [[Cliffhold]]. There, they were reprogrammed by [[Jaybo Hood]] as his servants.<ref name="Mystery of a Thousand Moons" />

Fifty of the best pilots attempted to leave Iego, but failed. Among them was [[Taquito]], whose death made the inhabitants believe the laser web was the work of [[Drol]], the so-called "phantom ruler" of Iego. After this had been going on for some time, [[Jedi]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] [[Mission to Iego|ventured]] to the planet in the [[starship]] ''[[Twilight]]'' in search of reeksa root, the only known cure for the deadly Blue Shadow Virus, in order to save people on [[Naboo]] who had been infected with a re-engineered strain of the disease and were trapped in an [[Trade Federation laboratory|underground bunker]]. Kenobi and Skywalker were assisted by a skeptical Hood, who was confident they would be as trapped on Iego as its inhabitants were. After venturing into a canyon to brave the reeksa, a [[carnivorous plant]], and retrieve some root, Kenobi and Skywalker attempted to leave, but were stopped by the [[LaserWeb Defense Station]], with Kenobi persuading his former apprentice to turn the ship around. However, with the help of Jaybo's vulture droids, the two Jedi destroyed the laser system, bringing freedom to Iego.<ref name="Mystery of a Thousand Moons" />

